  "observations": [
    "The ordinary full-context I offset is 4.60\u20134.66 s in both models. The same word becomes 4.88\u20134.92 s in the cropped-context ordinary offsets. Actual DTW events converge at 4.92\u20134.94 s across all three runs.",
    "Ordinary first-I offsets are 0\u20130.06/0.07 s while DTW events are 0.40/0.38 s and strong waveform onset is about 0.26 s. Ordinary offsets cannot be treated as exact phonetic timing.",
    "Acoustics at 4.60\u20134.68 s have RMS \u221246.12 dBFS and normalized autocorrelation 0.268, versus \u221219.81 dBFS / 0.724 at 4.81\u20134.94 s. The waveform and spectrogram show low-energy interphrase activity, then strong periodic voicing around 4.81 s.",
    "The evidence provides no positive identification of a quiet I at 4.60\u20134.68 s. Its earlier timestamp is likely an interpolation artifact. Low energy alone still cannot prove literal silence or exclude an extremely quiet phoneme.",
    "Small-model DTW collapses in and hospitality to 2.08 s elsewhere, demonstrating that DTW is not infallible. Cropped business is near a cut boundary and varies by 70 ms. Agreement from related Whisper models is corroboration, not independent phonetic ground truth."
  ],
  "judgment": {
    "quiet_I_at_4p60": "Not established; the earlier ordinary timestamp is unreliable. Evidence favors a later I associated with strong voicing near 4.81\u20134.94 s, with exact phonetic boundaries unresolved.",
    "pause_candidate": "The later wide-to-narrow mouth sequence is a reasonable comparison candidate. Matching a mouth maximum to the DTW event cannot itself establish better synchronization; anticipatory articulation remains a competing explanation for the original picture.",
    "next_evidence": "Independent dense/whole-A picture comparison and eventual normal-speed audiovisual review, preserving limits. No additional paid model call is implied."
  },
